2Ki 20:1 , Hezekiah, having received a message of death, by prayer has his life lengthened;
2Ki 20:8 , The sun goes ten degrees backward for a sign of that promise;
2Ki 20:12 , Berodach-baladan sending to visit Hezekiah, because of the wonder, has notice of his treasures;
2Ki 20:14 , Isaiah understanding thereof, foretells the Babylonian captivity;
2Ki 20:20 , Manasseh succeeds Hezekiah.
